Resume training from the last completed epoch (correctness: containerization / infrastructure limit).

Why: Modal limits one function attempt to 24 h and may restart a container (preemption). WLASL2000 needs
~32 h for 300 epochs, and run full-wlasl1000 already lost 125 epochs to a restart because train.py always
starts from epoch 0.

What: after every epoch, atomically write out-checkpoints/<experiment>/resume.pth with the model,
optimizer, scheduler, loop bookkeeping (epoch, accuracy histories, per-window top accuracies, checkpoint
index) and every RNG state train.py uses (random, numpy, torch CPU/CUDA, and the DataLoader generator g,
which also drives validation/test shuffling). On start, if that file exists, restore it and continue with
the next epoch. A run that is never interrupted executes exactly as before, plus one file write per epoch.

diff --git a/train.py b/train.py
index 746e59a..224ccab 100644
--- a/train.py
+++ b/train.py
